<resources>
    <!--
      The brand, for the frame Android draws BEFORE JavaScript exists.

      Without this the launcher shows a white sheet for the second or so it
      takes to start the runtime, and the app appears to flash before it opens.
      The colour has to be duplicated here because a native resource cannot
      read `src/theme/tokens.ts` — see `src/common/brand.ts` for the rest of
      what a rename has to touch.

      THE SHOPPING SIDE'S GREEN, and getting this wrong was a real bug rather
      than a preference. This app has two palettes and `ThemeProvider` decides
      which side wears which: shopping is EMERALD, working is CARMINE. Android
      cannot ask — this frame is painted before the process exists, let alone
      the store — so it is painted for the answer true of almost everybody and
      stated by the store listing from its first frame: customer.

      It was once #E94E00, and a shopper tapped an orange icon, waited behind
      an orange sheet and arrived in a green app. `splashAndIntro.test.ts`
      asserts this hex against `emeraldThemes.light.primary` so the two cannot
      drift again.
    -->
    <color name="brand">#10B981</color>
    <!--
      The launcher icon's ground. The same brand green, named separately
      because it is read by `mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml` and a colour
      the LAUNCHER holds is not the same fact as the colour the splash frame
      holds — one of them can change without the other.
    -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#10B981</color>
    <color name="brand_dark">#059669</color>
</resources>
